- `ADD_TEST OpticalConstructor.Tests.MaterialSourcesModelTests`

**How to implement.** The Online sources surface as a pure Elmish update over the import context, Update snapshot running off the UI thread with per-file progress and Cancel (001 §O; 001 §P: every user step is a semantic message; .spec-md §10.1 to §10.5: one click with Cancel, per-file progress, the completion message updates the model; the S13.1 brief: an 'Online sources…' search and fetch UI). It hosts the update as step 200 hosts an archive job and step 393 a fit, over `JobRunner.fs:startBackground`, `:updateJob` and `:JobModel`. New `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialSourcesView.fs`, `module OpticalConstructor.Ui.MaterialSourcesView`, compiled directly after `MaterialsWindowView.fs`: one `<Compile>` line in `OpticalConstructor.Ui.fsproj` and no comment. Its module doc and each declaration's doc are one to three lines citing spec 0050 S13.1. In order: (1) The host. `[<ReferenceEquality>] SourceSnapshotJobHandle = { cancelSourceSnapshot : unit -> unit }` and `[<ReferenceEquality>] SourceSnapshotJobHost = { startSourceSnapshot : (SourceSnapshotObserver -> Result<SourceRefresh, MaterialSourcePullError>) -> SourceSnapshotJobHandle }` with `static member posting (post : (unit -> unit) -> unit) (progressed : JobProgress -> unit) (ended : Result<SourceRefresh, MaterialSourcePullError> -> unit) : SourceSnapshotJobHost`, `onUiThread (progressed) (ended)`, `immediate (progressed) (ended)` and `inert`, each built as `KitArchiveJobHost`'s member of that name is (step 200): a `CancellationTokenSource` and a `Stopwatch` per job; each `SourceSnapshotProgress` told as `{ completed = JobStepCount filesDone.value; total = Some (JobStepCount filesTotal.value); elapsed = JobElapsed <the stopwatch's elapsed> }` (`JobRunner.fs:JobProgress`); a raise (`Error (JobRunExn e)`) ending as `Error (PullSourceErr (SourceSnapshotIoErr e.Message))`. (2) `[<ReferenceEquality>] MaterialSourcesContext = { imports : CatalogueImportContext; jobs : SourceSnapshotJobHost; pullsApplied : ControlCaption -> unit }`: the import seam the sources ride (step 444), the update's host, and the callback telling the window that opened it what the library gained, as `ImportDialogWindow` tells the Materials window (step 110). (3) `MaterialSourcesModel = { context : MaterialSourcesContext; shownSourceOpt : MaterialSourceName option; snapshotOpt : MaterialSourceVersion option; queryDraft : MaterialSourceQuery; hits : MaterialSourceHit list; job : JobModel<SourceSnapshotFileCount>; handleOpt : SourceSnapshotJobHandle option; status : ControlCaption option; error : MaterialSourcePullError option }`, each field documented, with `member this.shownSource : MaterialSourceProxy option`, the context's source of that name. (4) `MaterialSourcesMsg`, each case documented: `ShowMaterialSource of MaterialSourceName` | `SetSourceQueryDraft of MaterialSourceQuery` | `SearchMaterialSource of MaterialSourceQuery` | `PullSourceRecord of MaterialSourceRecordId` | `UpdateSourceSnapshot` | `CancelSourceSnapshot` | `SourceSnapshotProgressed of JobProgress` | `SourceSnapshotEnded of Result<SourceRefresh, MaterialSourcePullError>`. (5) `initMaterialSources (context : MaterialSourcesContext) : MaterialSourcesModel` shows the first of `imports.materialSources` (`None` when there is none), reads its `snapshotVersion ()` (an error held as `PullSourceErr`), and holds an empty query, no hit, the job `initModel` (`JobRunner.fs:185`), no handle and no status. (6) `updateMaterialSources (msg : MaterialSourcesMsg) (m : MaterialSourcesModel) : MaterialSourcesModel`: `ShowMaterialSource name` shows that source, reading its snapshot version and clearing hits, status and error (an unknown name changes nothing); `SetSourceQueryDraft q` sets the draft; `SearchMaterialSource q` answers the shown source's `searchRecords q` as `hits` and clears the error, or holds `PullSourceErr` with no hit; `PullSourceRecord r` is `imports.pullRecord <the shown source> r` (step 444): `Ok results` sets `status` to their captions joined by a space, clears the error and calls `context.pullsApplied` with that status, and `Error e` holds `e`; `UpdateSourceSnapshot` while the job runs changes nothing, and otherwise starts `imports.updateSourceSnapshot <the shown source>` through `context.jobs.startSourceSnapshot`, passes the job through `updateJob StartRequested`, holds the handle and clears status and error; `CancelSourceSnapshot` calls the handle's `cancelSourceSnapshot` while the job runs; `SourceSnapshotProgressed p` is `updateJob (ProgressReported p)`; `SourceSnapshotEnded (Ok (SourceRefreshed info))` is `updateJob (RunCompleted info.snapshot.files)` with no handle, `snapshotOpt = Some info.snapshot.version` and `status` the refresh's caption, and then calls `context.pullsApplied` of it, so the Materials window re-renders with any new version and no reload (.spec-md §10.4); `SourceSnapshotEnded (Ok SourceRefreshCancelled)` is `updateJob RunCancelled` with no handle and the status `The snapshot update was cancelled; the held snapshot is unchanged.`; and `SourceSnapshotEnded (Error e)` returns the job to `Idle` with no handle and holds `e`. No queue, retry or second job is added: one update at a time. (7) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each a one-line doc: `MaterialSourcePullError.caption` (its `describe`); `SourcePullResult.caption`: `Pulled <name> as version 1.`, `<name>: the record changed; pulled as version <n>.`, `<name> is unchanged at version <n>.` or `<name>: the snapshot no longer lists <record>; left at version <n>.`; `SourceRefreshInfo.caption`: `Snapshot <version> holds <files> files.` followed by each pull's caption, joined by spaces; and `ConstructorUiId.materialSourceChoice (name : MaterialSourceName)` (`MaterialSourceChoice_<name>`), `materialSourceHitRow (record : MaterialSourceRecordId)` (`MaterialSourceHit_<record>`) and `materialSourcePullButton (record : MaterialSourceRecordId)` (`MaterialSourcePull_<record>`). `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, a new group after the Materials window's under `// --- The Online sources window (MaterialSourcesView, MaterialSourcesWindow). ---`, each with a one-line doc and the PascalCase of its name as its text: `materialSourceSnapshotText`, `materialSourceUpdateButton`, `materialSourceUpdateProgressBar`, `materialSourceUpdateProgressText`, `materialSourceUpdateCancelButton`, `materialSourceQueryBox`, `materialSourceSearchButton`, `materialSourceHitList` and `materialSourcesStatusText`. (8) `materialSourcesView (m : MaterialSourcesModel) (dispatch : MaterialSourcesMsg -> unit) : IView`, a pure projection: a `ScrollViewer` over a `MinWidthPanel` of minimum width 520, both scroll bars `Auto`, as `dataLocationsView` scrolls (step 193), over a vertical `StackPanel`. With no source it holds only `No online material source is configured.` in a `TextBlock` carrying `materialSourcesStatusText`. Otherwise it holds, in order: a row of one `MaterialsWindowView.verbButton` per source (`materialSourceChoice`, the shown one on `positiveBackground`, sending `ShowMaterialSource`); a `DockPanel` whose right side is `Update snapshot` (`materialSourceUpdateButton`, disabled while the job runs, sending `UpdateSourceSnapshot`) and whose fill is a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `materialSourceSnapshotText`: `Snapshot <version>`, or `No snapshot yet; Update snapshot downloads the database.`; while the job runs, a progress row of a `ProgressBar` carrying `materialSourceUpdateProgressBar` (minimum 0, maximum 1, the progress's fraction, indeterminate before the first file), the job's `progressText` (or `Downloading…` before the first file) in a `TextBlock` carrying `materialSourceUpdateProgressText`, and `Cancel` (`materialSourceUpdateCancelButton`, a `MaterialsWindowView.actionButton` on `negativeBackground`, sending `CancelSourceSnapshot`); a `DockPanel` whose right side is `Search` (`materialSourceSearchButton`, sending `SearchMaterialSource m.queryDraft`) and whose fill is a `TextBox` carrying `materialSourceQueryBox` with the draft's text, sending `SetSourceQueryDraft` on each change and `SearchMaterialSource` on Enter; a vertical `StackPanel` carrying `materialSourceHitList` with one `DockPanel` per hit carrying `materialSourceHitRow`, its right side `Pull` (`materialSourcePullButton`, sending `PullSourceRecord`) and its fill the semi-bold name over the record's text; and, when either is set, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `materialSourcesStatusText` with the error's caption in `MaterialsWindowView.messageColor`, or else the status. Every id is the control's `Name` and `AutomationId`. Tests: new `OpticalConstructor.Tests/MaterialSourcesModelTests.fs`, `module MaterialSourcesModelTests`, appended at the end of the compile list with no comment, over an import context built as step 444's tests build theirs, its `materialSources` set by record update to step 443's double holding the Silicon record at `2026-11-01`, a `pullsApplied` recording its captions, and `SourceSnapshotJobHost.immediate` whose `progressed` and `ended` the fact feeds back through `updateMaterialSources` in order, or a test-local host recording its job and the cancels of its handle. `the surface opens on the first source and its held snapshot`: `shownSourceOpt` names `Test source`, `snapshotOpt` is `2026-11-01` and there is no hit; over an import context with no source, `shownSourceOpt` is `None`. `SearchMaterialSource lists the hits the shown source finds`: `silicon` lists the Silicon hit; a double holding no snapshot holds `PullSourceErr (SourceSnapshotMissingErr _)` and no hit. `PullSourceRecord pulls the record and tells the opener what the library gained`: `PullSourceRecord` of the Silicon record sets the status `Pulled Si (Silicon), Aspnes as version 1.`, recorded once by `pullsApplied`, and the import seam holds the material. `UpdateSourceSnapshot runs the update with per-file progress, then refreshes the pulls and tells the opener`: after that pull, with `2026-11-04` published holding the record under another hash, `UpdateSourceSnapshot` over `immediate` reports 1 of 1 files, completes with `snapshotOpt` `2026-11-04`, and its status, recorded by `pullsApplied`, names version 2; over the recording host, a second `UpdateSourceSnapshot` while the first job is recorded starts none. `a cancelled update keeps the held snapshot and says so`: over the recording host, `CancelSourceSnapshot` records one cancel, and `SourceSnapshotEnded (Ok SourceRefreshCancelled)` leaves `snapshotOpt` `2026-11-01`, the cancelled status and the job not running. `a failed update tells why`: `SourceSnapshotEnded (Error (PullSourceErr (SourceDownloadErr "offline")))` holds that error with the job not running.

**Acceptance.** After the surface lands, `updateMaterialSources` MUST search, pull through `pullRecord` and run Update snapshot through the injected `SourceSnapshotJobHost` with per-file progress and Cancel, one update at a time, telling the opener every caption a pull or an update produces; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `the surface opens on the first source and its held snapshot`, `SearchMaterialSource lists the hits the shown source finds`, `PullSourceRecord pulls the record and tells the opener what the library gained`, `UpdateSourceSnapshot runs the update with per-file progress, then refreshes the pulls and tells the opener`, `a cancelled update keeps the held snapshot and says so` and `a failed update tells why`, the count rising by 6; ui-smoke MUST pass; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s43 invariants MUST pass.
